# Three keys that print as `east 1`, and only two of them are equal. The
# headline quotes the duplicate with `repr` and so cannot say which two -- and
# it does not have to. The caret is on the second and the note carries the
# first, and a position is unambiguous in a way no rendering of a value is.
# This message is why revealing was not applied to all five messages that
# quote a value: it needs nothing.
let m = {"east 1": 1, "east\u{a0}1": 2, "east 1": 3}
